# How git handles line endings in this repository.
#
# Windows tools (including pandas running on Windows) end lines with CRLF
# (\r\n); macOS and Linux use LF (\n). Without a rule here, the same file
# written on two different systems looks 100% changed to git.
#
# text=auto: store every text file with LF *inside the repository*, and
# convert back to the local convention on checkout. Files on disk keep the
# form your tools expect, while the repository stays consistent across
# operating systems.

* text=auto
